speechtext:
I should like to ask a question of the government. I hold in my hand a resolution passed by the trades and labour council of Trois Rivieres, Quebec. It reads as follows:
Whereas the ration of butter actually available is totally insufficient for the worker who brings his meal at the plant;
Whereas such a rationing, besides allowing an insufficient quantity of butter might prove to be a serious impeachment to the war effort of the worker-
